.#-----------------------------------------------------
.input|xwiki/2.1
.# Standalone code macros located in table cells are rendered inline since Markdown table cells can only contain
.# inline content: as code spans when their language is "none", and using the macro syntax otherwise (except when the
.# macro syntax can't be used, e.g. for a content containing a backtick that doesn't start a code span, in which case a
.# code span is used and the parameters are lost). Line endings are replaced by spaces (as for verbatim). Consecutive
.# code spans are separated by a space so that they're not read back as a single code span. See code11.test for the
.# parsing of the generated Markdown.
.#-----------------------------------------------------
|=a|=b
|x|(((
{{code language="java"}}
int i = 0;
int j = 1;
{{/code}}
)))
|y|(((
{{code}}a`b{{/code}}

{{code language="none"}}c{{/code}}

{{{d}}}
)))
.#-----------------------------------------------------
.expect|markdown/1.2
.#-----------------------------------------------------
|  a  | b |
| --- | --- |
|  x  | {{code language="java"}}int i = 0; int j = 1;{{/code}} |
|  y  | ``a`b`` `c`<br/><br/>{{verbatim}}d{{/verbatim}} |
